Fix BOOLEAN syscall arguments being read as full dwords on x86_64

Wine's PE side is compiled for the Microsoft x64 ABI, where the upper bits of
an argument narrower than 64 bits are *undefined* — the caller may write only
the low byte. The unix side is compiled for the System V AMD64 ABI, where the
caller is required to zero-extend sub-word arguments to 32 bits, so the
compiler is entitled to test the full 32-bit register.
__wine_syscall_dispatcher forwards the raw argument slot between the two, so
that guarantee does not hold and stale stack garbage in the high bits makes a
BOOLEAN argument read as TRUE when the caller passed FALSE.

Observed on macOS/aarch64 (Rosetta) with a PE side built by llvm-mingw, which
emits

    movb   $0x0,0x20(%rsp)      ; restart = FALSE, one byte only
    mov    $0x1,%r9b            ; single_entry = TRUE, low byte only

for kernelbase's GetLogicalDrives(), while the unix side compiles
`restart ? 0 : *context` to

    testl  %r8d,%r8d            ; tests 32 bits

With garbage above the low byte, `restart` reads TRUE, `index` is pinned to 0,
and GetLogicalDrives()'s

    while (!NtQueryDirectoryObject( handle, info, sizeof(data), 1, 0, &ctx, &len ))

never terminates: the same \DosDevices entry is returned forever. Because the
thread doing this holds ntdll's loader lock (it is inside a DllMain), every
other thread then times out in LdrResolveDelayLoadedAPI on loader_section, so
the process appears to deadlock rather than spin.

CrossOver's own build is unaffected only because its PE compiler happens to
emit `movl $0x0,0x20(%rsp)` / `mov $0x1,%r9d`, zero-extending both arguments.
That is luck, not a guarantee.

Read the argument a byte at a time so the value is correct under either ABI.

Note: 40 syscall entry points take a sub-word argument and are subject to the
same hazard (NtWaitForSingleObject's `alertable`, NtQueryDirectoryFile's
`single_entry`/`restart_scan`, ...). This patch fixes the two that are proven
to hang BeamNG.drive; the general fix belongs in the dispatcher.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -2070,6 +2070,21 @@
     }
     SERVER_END_REQ;
     return ret;
+}
+
+
+/* The PE side of Wine is Microsoft-x64-ABI code, where the high bits of an
+ * argument narrower than 64 bits are undefined and a caller may write only the
+ * low byte.  The unix side is System-V code, where the caller is required to
+ * zero-extend such arguments and the compiler is therefore entitled to test the
+ * full 32-bit register.  __wine_syscall_dispatcher forwards the raw argument
+ * slot between the two, so that guarantee does not hold across the syscall
+ * boundary and stale garbage in the high bits reads as TRUE.  Force a
+ * byte-wide read of the incoming value.
+ */
+static inline int syscall_bool_arg( BOOLEAN value )
+{
+    return *(volatile unsigned char *)&value != 0;
 }
 
 
@@ -2081,7 +2096,8 @@
                                         ULONG *context, ULONG *ret_size )
 {
     unsigned int status, i, count, total_len, pos, used_size, used_count, strpool_head;
-    ULONG index = restart ? 0 : *context;
+    ULONG index = syscall_bool_arg( restart ) ? 0 : *context;
+    const int single = syscall_bool_arg( single_entry );
     struct directory_entry *entries;
 
     if (!(entries = malloc( size ))) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
@@ -2090,7 +2106,7 @@
     {
         req->handle = wine_server_obj_handle( handle );
         req->index = index;
-        req->max_count = single_entry ? 1 : UINT_MAX;
+        req->max_count = single ? 1 : UINT_MAX;
         wine_server_set_reply( req, entries, size );
         status = wine_server_call( req );
         count = reply->count;
@@ -2159,7 +2175,7 @@
         return STATUS_NO_MORE_ENTRIES;
     }
 
-    if (single_entry && !used_count)
+    if (single && !used_count)
     {
         if (ret_size) *ret_size = 2 * sizeof(*buffer) + 2 * sizeof(WCHAR) + total_len;
         return STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;
